  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n・{提案|ていあん}する (to propose, to suggest)\n・{提案|ていあん}を{受|う}ける (to receive a proposal)\n・{提案|ていあん}を{受|う}け{入|い}れる (to accept a proposal)\n・{提案|ていあん}を{却下|きゃっか}する (to reject a proposal)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUND WORDS:\n・{提案|ていあん}{書|しょ} (proposal document)\n・{提案|ていあん}{者|しゃ} (proposer)\n・{法案|ほうあん}{提案|ていあん} (submission of a bill)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{提案|ていあん}: Proposal (formal, business/official contexts)\n・{提言|ていげん}: Recommendation (more formal, policy suggestions)\n・{案|あん}: Plan, idea (less formal)",
